What is Cron?

Cron is a Linux scheduler used to run scripts automatically at specified times.

Why DevOps Engineers Use Cron?
Automated Backups
Log Cleanup
Health Monitoring
Security Checks
Database Dumps
Report Generation
View Existing Cron Jobs
crontab -l
Edit Cron Jobs
crontab -e
Cron Syntax
* * * * * command
│ │ │ │ │
│ │ │ │ └── Day of Week (0-7)
│ │ │ └──── Month
│ │ └────── Day of Month
│ └──────── Hour
└────────── Minute
Examples

Run every minute:

* * * * * /home/scripts/health.sh

Run every day at 2 AM:

0 2 * * * /home/scripts/backup.sh

Run every Sunday:

0 0 * * 0 /home/scripts/weekly-report.sh
Real-Time DevOps Example

Disk Monitoring Every 5 Minutes

*/5 * * * * /opt/scripts/disk-monitor.sh
